1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,160
July 20, 1944.

2
00:00:02,548 --> 00:00:04,118
Deep inside Nazi Germany,

3
00:00:04,388 --> 00:00:06,348
a group of German officers prepared to do

4
00:00:06,348 --> 00:00:08,878
the unthinkable: assassinate Adolf Hitler.

5
00:00:09,241 --> 00:00:11,141
At the center of the plot was Colonel Claus

6
00:00:11,141 --> 00:00:12,331
von Stauffenberg.

7
00:00:12,553 --> 00:00:14,443
Carrying a bomb inside his briefcase,

8
00:00:14,633 --> 00:00:16,523
he entered Hitler's heavily guarded headquarters:

9
00:00:17,033 --> 00:00:17,783
the Wolf's Lair.

10
00:00:18,130 --> 00:00:19,460
During a military briefing,

11
00:00:19,530 --> 00:00:21,110
he placed the briefcase beneath the conference

12
00:00:21,110 --> 00:00:23,960
table, excused himself, and walked out.

13
00:00:24,223 --> 00:00:26,243
Minutes later, an explosion tore through

14
00:00:26,243 --> 00:00:26,733
the room.

15
00:00:26,983 --> 00:00:29,383
But Hitler survived. The briefcase had apparently

16
00:00:29,383 --> 00:00:31,673
been moved behind a massive table support,

17
00:00:31,863 --> 00:00:32,973
shielding him from the blast.

18
00:00:33,487 --> 00:00:34,797
Believing Hitler was dead,

19
00:00:35,167 --> 00:00:37,047
Stauffenberg rushed back to Berlin to launch

20
00:00:37,047 --> 00:00:37,997
Operation Valkyrie.

21
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:40,100
It was originally an emergency military

22
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:42,940
plan. The conspirators had secretly turned

23
00:00:42,940 --> 00:00:44,430
it into a blueprint for a coup.

24
00:00:44,758 --> 00:00:46,408
Troops began receiving orders.

25
00:00:46,978 --> 00:00:48,188
Government buildings were targeted.

26
00:00:48,498 --> 00:00:49,548
The takeover had begun.

27
00:00:49,809 --> 00:00:52,009
Then came the devastating news: Hitler was

28
00:00:52,009 --> 00:00:53,579
alive. The operation collapsed.

29
00:00:54,078 --> 00:00:55,958
That same night, Stauffenberg and several

30
00:00:55,958 --> 00:00:57,328
conspirators were executed.

31
00:00:57,898 --> 00:00:59,818
Their attempt to overthrow the Nazi regime

32
00:00:59,818 --> 00:01:00,568
had failed.

33
00:01:00,859 --> 00:01:02,699
But July 20, 1944,

34
00:01:02,699 --> 00:01:05,649
proved that even inside Hitler's own military,

35
00:01:06,139 --> 00:01:07,599
there were men willing to risk everything

36
00:01:07,599 --> 00:01:08,529
to stop him.

